1) download orca-6.1.0-f.0_linux_x86-64_openmpi41.tar.xz from https://www.faccts.de/customer
2) extract by using command: tar -xJvf orca-6.1.0-f.0_linux_x86-64_openmpi41.tar.xz 
3) go to bin by commands:           cd orca-6.1.0-f.0_linux_x86-64     then   cd bin
4) copy the present directory by using command : pwd
5) copy the directory for example  : /home/durjoy/all_soft/ORCA/orca-6.1.0-f.0_linux_x86-64/bin (your path can be different from me)

6) copy and pest the following line at the last of your .bashrc script 

## ORCA orca-6.1.0
export PATH=/home/durjoy/all_soft/ORCA/orca-6.1.0-f.0_linux_x86-64/bin:$PATH
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$/home/durjoy/all_soft/ORCA/orca-6.1.0-f.0_linux_x86-64/bin"


7) paste your directory in 2nd line and 4th line of the above where the  /home/durjoy/all_soft/ORCA/orca-6.1.0-f.0_linux_x86-64/bin exist    directory exists

8) save the baschrc script.

9) creat a orca input file(ethanol.inp) like the following (here 6 is the number of processor you are using . you can use different according to your number of processors): 

